// Bot FUNCTION (not a handler) -- the target of the welcome message's
// "Send me a new code" button.
//
// Why it exists: a pairing code lasts ten minutes, and until now the only way
// to get another was to unsubscribe and resubscribe. Someone who read the
// welcome message on their phone and reached a terminal an hour later had no
// route forward. Measured: a colleague collected three dead codes that way
// and never paired at all.
//
// Create this in the bot builder as a function named exactly (Cliq function
// names allow letters only -- no underscores):
//     REPLACE_WITH_NEWCODE_FUNCTION_NAME
//
// The name is per ENVIRONMENT, not per bot. Cliq functions are account-level,
// so every bot in the account sees the same list -- a test bot reusing the
// production function would issue production codes with the production
// secret. Same reasoning as REPLACE_WITH_FUNCTION_NAME.

payload = Map();
payload.put("cliq_user", user.get("id"));
// The relay refuses a code without one, and it is how a tap is attributed.
// Cliq grants a bot the subscriber's address only by a consent that lapses
// after 60 days, so this can be null -- the relay answers 400 and the message
// below says what to do about it.
payload.put("email", user.get("email"));

headers = Map();
headers.put("Content-Type", "application/json");
headers.put("X-Relay-Secret", "REPLACE_WITH_RELAY_INBOUND_SECRET");

// One return at the top level: Deluge does not count a return inside a try,
// and reports the error against the try line rather than the return.
response = Map();
try
{
	result = invokeurl
	[
		url: "REPLACE_WITH_RELAY_BASE/refresh-code"
		type: POST
		parameters: payload.toString()
		headers: headers
	];

	// invokeurl does NOT raise on an HTTP error, so the body is the only
	// signal -- a 400 or 403 arrives here looking like a successful call with
	// no `code` in it.
	code = result.get("code");

	if(code == null)
	{
		response.put("text", "I couldn't generate a code just now. Unsubscribing and subscribing again will also issue one.");
	}
	else
	{
		msg = "Here's a fresh pairing code. Inside Claude Code:\n";
		msg = msg + "```\n/claude-cliq:pair " + code + " REPLACE_WITH_RELAY_BASE\n```\n";
		// Said every time, because the whole reason someone taps this button
		// is that they did not know the last one had run out.
		msg = msg + "Good for 10 minutes. This replaces any earlier code — the one in the welcome message no longer works.";
		response.put("text", msg);
	}
}
catch (e)
{
	response.put("text", "Couldn't reach Claude Code: " + e.toString());
}
return response;
